  "symptom_nitrogen": "• Older leaves turn pale green or yellow\n• Stunted growth\n• Thin and weak stems",
  "treatment_nitrogen": "• Fast: Add Liquid Fish Emulsion and Coffee grounds to the soil\n• Long-Term: Add blood meal or compost",
  "symptom_phosphorus": "• Dark green or purplish leaves\n• Delayed growth\n• Poor root development",
  "treatment_phosphorus": "• Fast: High-P Water Soluble Feed\n• Long-Term: Bone meal & check pH",
  "symptom_potassium": "• Leaf edges turn yellow or brown (scorching)\n• Weak stems\n• Increased susceptibility to disease",
  "treatment_potassium": "• Fast: Add Banana peels; Add Seaweed Extract\n• Long-Term: Greensand or kelp meal",
  "symptom_calcium": "• New leaves are deformed or curled\n• Tip burn (especially in lettuce)\n• Poor root growth",
  "treatment_calcium": "• Fast: Add eggshells into the soil and water consistently\n• Long-Term: Gypsum or Dolomitic Lime",
  "symptom_magnesium": "• Yellowing between leaf veins (chlorosis)\n• Older leaves affected first\n• Leaves may curl upward",
  "treatment_magnesium": "• Fast: Epsom Salt foliar spray\n• Long-Term: Dolomitic Lime",
  "symptom_powdery_mildew": "• White powdery spots on leaves and stems\n• Curling or yellowing of leaves\n• Stunted plant growth",
  "treatment_powdery_mildew": "• Fast: Apply Neem oil or Potassium Bicarbonate\n• Long-Term: Improve airflow and reduce humidity",
  "symptom_downy_mildew": "• Light green or yellow spots on top of leaves\n• Fluffy grayish/purplish growth on leaf undersides",
  "treatment_downy_mildew": "• Fast: Apply Copper-based fungicide\n• Long-Term: Ensure proper plant spacing",
  "symptom_bacterial_leaf_spot": "• Small, dark, water-soaked spots\n• Lesions may have a yellow halo\n• Spots may merge, killing large leaf areas",
  "treatment_bacterial_leaf_spot": "• Fast: Apply Copper bactericides\n• Long-Term: Remove diseased plants and debris immediately",
  "symptom_lettuce_mosaic_virus": "• Mottled green and yellow leaf pattern\n• Stunted growth and ruffled leaf edges\n• Vein clearing or yellowing",
  "treatment_lettuce_mosaic_virus": "• Fast: Remove and destroy infected plants immediately (No cure)\n• Long-Term: Control aphids (vectors) and use certified disease-free seed",
  "symptom_aphids": "• Small, clustered insects on leaf undersides\n• Leaves may curl, yellow, or become distorted\n• Sticky honeydew residue on leaves",
  "treatment_aphids": "• Fast: Spray with insecticidal soap or Neem oil\n• Long-Term: Introduce beneficial insects like ladybugs",
  "symptom_caterpillars": "• Large, irregular chewed holes in leaves\n• Dark droppings (frass) left on the plant\n• Rapid defoliation of the lettuce head",
  "treatment_caterpillars": "• Fast: Handpick them off or apply Bt (Bacillus thuringiensis) spray\n• Long-Term: Use floating row covers to prevent egg-laying",
  "symptom_slugs": "• Irregular holes chewed in the middle of leaves\n• Shiny, silvery slime trails left behind\n• Mostly active at night or in very damp conditions",
  "treatment_slugs": "• Fast: Set up shallow beer traps or apply diatomaceous earth\n• Long-Term: Reduce surface moisture and use copper tape barriers",
  "droplet_warning": "• WARNING: Prolonged moisture on leaves creates an ideal breeding ground for fungal diseases and attracts pests like slugs.",
  "droplet_action": "• Fast: Gently shake or wipe excess water from the leaves\n• Long-Term: Water lettuce at the base early in the morning",
